The handler always increments `actionRefreshKey` and returns `{ reload: true }` even when the action doesn’t request a refresh. This ignores `action.refreshAfter` and may cause unnecessary DetailView remounts/state loss for actions that shouldn’t refresh the record. Consider only triggering the refresh (and setting `reload`) when `action.refreshAfter` is true (or when the handler actually mutated record data).
```suggestion
      const shouldRefresh = action.refreshAfter === true;
      if (shouldRefresh) {
        setActionRefreshKey(k => k + 1);
      }
      return { success: true, reload: shouldRefresh };
```

Required-field validation uses `!values[param.name]`, which treats valid falsy values (e.g. `0` for number, `false` for boolean) as missing and will incorrectly block submission. Consider checking specifically for `undefined`/`null`/empty-string instead (and handling arrays/objects appropriately if those types are supported).
```suggestion
  const isMissingValue = (value: unknown): boolean => {
    if (value === undefined || value === null) {
      return true;
    }
    if (typeof value === 'string') {
      return value.trim() === '';
    }
    if (Array.isArray(value)) {
      return value.length === 0;
    }
    return false;
  };

  const handleSubmit = () => {
    // Validate required fields
    const newErrors: Record<string, boolean> = {};
    for (const param of state.params) {
      if (param.required) {
        const value = values[param.name];
        if (isMissingValue(value)) {
          newErrors[param.name] = true;
        }
```
